{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/647029-2e-riding-the-wave-mechanics","id":647029,"title":"[2E] \"Riding the Wave\" Mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-31T12:02:51-07:00","id":647029,"title":"[2E] \"Riding the Wave\" Mechanics","content":"There's something I didn't understand after reading the rules for resisting Frenzy versus Riding the Wave:<br /> <br /> - When a vampire rolls for resisting Frenzy, you roll once, as a Resolve + Composure pool plus an equipment bonus equal to the number of willpower points spent in resisting Frenzy during the previous turns.<br /> <br /> - When trying to Ride the Wave, a vampire spends a willpower point to let him roll his Resolve + Composure pool, and this process keeps going on as long as WP is spent as an Extended roll, until it reaches 5 successes.<br /> <br /> Is my interpretation correct about these mechanics?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T12:14:17-07:00","id":647057,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T12:22:18-07:00","id":647088,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot, Charlaquin! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T13:26:59-07:00","id":647145,"title":"","content":"Note that as you can only spend 1 Willpower per turn, you can only roll once per turn for Ride the Wave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:28:38-07:00","id":649056,"title":"","content":"And you also get the benefits of Riding the Wave before you hit that fifth success. You just lose control of the frenzy if you fail a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T21:34:40-07:00","id":652093,"title":"","content":"@MCN: Citation on that one? Not saying you are wrong, just want to be able to point to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T00:43:44-07:00","id":654865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/647029-2e-riding-the-wave-mechanics?p=652093#post652093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@MCN: Citation on that one? Not saying you are wrong, just want to be able to point to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't cite it because I'm not at my computer, but that's how I intended it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T03:38:42-07:00","id":654985,"title":"","content":"Really? I guess something got lost in editing then because that's precisely what the book says <i>doesn't</i> happen. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To ride the wave, spend a Willpower point, and make the<br /> normal Resolve + Composure resistance roll. The Willpower<br /> point does not add to this roll. Success holds off the frenzy for<br /> a turn as if she\u2019d spent Willpower to fight the frenzy. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T03:59:35-07:00","id":655016,"title":"","content":"Also, does it mean that each roll for riding the wave gets a cumulative +1, since it works as i'm using willpower to fight the frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","user":"TittoPaolo210","date":". 09-07-2015, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T16:31:27-07:00","id":673530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/647029-2e-riding-the-wave-mechanics?p=655016#post655016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, does it mean that each roll for riding the wave gets a cumulative +1, since it works as i'm using willpower to fight the frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would; resisting frenzy is taking an act of will to hold it off, and the longer you can hold it back, the easier time you might have getting the Beast back into its cage, so to speak. Meanwhile, when Riding the Wave, you're doing the exact opposite\u2014pushing yourself to goad this part of you that you normally <i>really</i> don't want to let loose.<br /> <br /> (Side note: I could have sworn that going into Frenzy in any way at all means you lose your Defense bonus, but I can't seem to find any mention of it in VtR 2 / B&amp;S. Anyone remember this or am I just imagining things?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T23:24:33-07:00","id":673883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/647029-2e-riding-the-wave-mechanics?p=673530#post673530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Side note: I could have sworn that going into Frenzy in any way at all means you lose your Defense bonus, but I can't seem to find any mention of it in VtR 2 / B&amp;S. Anyone remember this or am I just imagining things?)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a rule, but I could see a Frenzying vampire favoring all-out attacks over keeping her defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T03:17:27-07:00","id":674009,"title":"","content":"Depends on the goal the beast is set to pursue. &quot;Kill that guy&quot; will probably result in all out attacks, but &quot;get out of this building alive&quot; won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T12:20:54-07:00","id":674476,"title":"","content":"Oh, OK, wait, hold on, back up, rewind...<br /> You can use Ride The Wave without an action on your turn, roll Resolve + Composure, get a success, and then behave <i>for that turn</i> as if you were in a full, controlled, Ride The Wave Frenzy? <br /> THAT'S HUGE! And the downside is, when your dice-pool turns are up and you've still not gathered a total of five successes, you &quot;let go&quot;?<br /> DAMN! NICE!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T19:08:06-07:00","id":674793,"title":"","content":"Frenzy reads to work as follows.<br /> <br /> After something happens to trigger a frenzy roll, the vampire can roll or spend a point of willpower to delay the roll for a turn. The vampire can continue delaying the roll as long as they spend willpower each turn. When the roll is finally made all the spent willpower counts as bonus die for the roll. If the roll succeeds, no frenzy. If the roll ends in failure, frenzy. There is only one roll.<br /> <br /> Riding the Wave differs in that there are series of rolls as long as willpower is spent each turn and at least one success is rolled. If 5 successes are rolled then the vampire has control over the frenzy. If the vampire stops spending willpower, runs out of willpower, or fails a roll then it is a normal frenzy.<br /> <br /> The &quot;bonuses of riding the wave&quot; don't include frenzy bonuses until 5 successes are rolled as written. It isn't clear whether David Hill intended frenzy bonuses to be included before the 5 successes or not by his statement here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T19:13:18-07:00","id":674797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/647029-2e-riding-the-wave-mechanics?p=674793#post674793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frenzy reads to work as follows.<br /> <br /> After something happens to trigger a frenzy roll, the vampire can roll or spend a point of willpower to delay the roll for a turn. The vampire can continue delaying the roll as long as they spend willpower each turn. When the roll is finally made all the spent willpower counts as bonus die for the roll. If the roll succeeds, no frenzy. If the roll ends in failure, frenzy. There is only one roll.<br /> <br /> Riding the Wave differs in that there are series of rolls as long as willpower is spent each turn and at least one success is rolled. If 5 successes are rolled then the vampire has control over the frenzy. If the vampire stops spending willpower, runs out of willpower, or fails a roll then it is a normal frenzy.<br /> <br /> The &quot;bonuses of riding the wave&quot; don't include frenzy bonuses until 5 successes are rolled as written. It isn't clear whether David Hill intended frenzy bonuses to be included before the 5 successes or not by his statement here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, looks like that was pretty clearly his intent. It's also pretty clearly not how it works as written, so it seems likely that it got changed at some point in development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T19:57:27-07:00","id":674860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/647029-2e-riding-the-wave-mechanics?p=674797#post674797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, looks like that was pretty clearly his intent. It's also pretty clearly not how it works as written, so it seems likely that it got changed at some point in development.</div> </div> </div> </div>MCN was a bit vague on what the benefits of riding the wave were when Hill agreed with it. Nothing vague about the book. Actually, there is nothing wrong if MCN and Hill intended what others have assumed from their words, which is a fair interpretation. I'm not actually stating a position on that. Clearly there is confusion. I don't know which way is the right one. Normally, I would say a writer's input is good enough as a citation, but I think we need something more when it seemingly contradicts the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:03:37-07:00","id":675644,"title":"","content":"I wasn't vague. I was pretty clear in what I said - you get the benefits as soon as you start trying to roll. &quot;I'm riding the wave.&quot; &quot;Okay, benefits start now, don't fail or you lose control.&quot; Can't get much more clear than that.<br /> <br /> The passage might be unclear, because I've talked to others who've read it the same way I have. If we have multiple people who are reading the same passage differently, then I'm going to lean towards the book itself being unclear, and not the people who disagree with your reading.<br /> <br /> You have others who are reading differently than you. You have the writers who very clearly stated their intent of the passage. What more do you want? We have a pretty clear answer on how its meant to operate. If you don't like it, then make the ruling for your table, and game on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:27:29-07:00","id":675698,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry but what part of &quot;Success holds off the frenzy for a turn as if she\u2019d spent Willpower to fight the frenzy&quot; is ambiguous?<br /> <br /> Normally, when you spend willpower, you don't frenzy. Therefore, if you <i>do </i>get the benefits of frenzy, it's <i>not &quot;</i>as if you'd spent Willpower to fight the frenzy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:42:57-07:00","id":675721,"title":"","content":"I'm not here to give a rules argument; in my experience, these boards just degenerate into calling each other's reading stupid or something. That's not what I'm here for. <br /> <br /> I flat out said how I read it. I was not unclear in any way. Others have read it the same way as I did independantly. We have the word of an author on his intent.<br /> <br /> Run it the way you want that supports the themes and style you want. There's no fun police to tell you you're doing it wrong. Cheers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-23-2015, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T16:43:21-07:00","id":675796,"title":"","content":"How would it even work that way? In Frenzy the beast gets a goal. If you ride the wave, you set it. If you don't the Beast does.<br /> <br /> If riding the wave allows you to frenzy for a few turns before the roll is settled, who sets the goal? Does the goal suddenly change if you fail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T19:36:24-07:00","id":675960,"title":"","content":"When you say &quot;benefits&quot; but don't specify what the benefits are, you are being vague. You clarified what you meant. I thought that was probably what you meant, but I didn't want to put words in your mouth. A person can disregard what the book says if they want. It isn't my concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T18:12:39-07:00","id":677103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/647029-2e-riding-the-wave-mechanics?p=675796#post675796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would it even work that way? In Frenzy the beast gets a goal. If you ride the wave, you set it. If you don't the Beast does.<br /> <br /> If riding the wave allows you to frenzy for a few turns before the roll is settled, who sets the goal? Does the goal suddenly change if you fail?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always require there to be a goal before the rolls start. After all, you don't need to roll unless the Beast has an objective in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}